| 8 | 合成時に意味汚染がない (no semantic contamination at composition time) | PARTIAL | Updated from PARTIAL (stays PARTIAL, not ALIVE -- see scope note below): a second, real automated gate now closes the output-path-collision gap's sibling, term/individual-level contamination, for the two conflict shapes it actually checks. `.specify/gates/cross-pack-contamination.rq` is a SPARQL SELECT wired into this repo's own root `ggen.toml` (`[validation].gates`, confirmed live: a real `ggen sync run --dry-run` against this workspace's actual composed graph passes it with zero violations) that refuses the sync if any subject IRI in the union graph carries conflicting `rdf:type` assertions or conflicting values for a known functional property (`ccn:principleNumber`/`ccn:mechanized` from ggen-constitution-pack, `grp:artifactPath` from this pack -- real properties, not hypothetical ones). `crates/ggen-engine/tests/pack_e2e.rs`'s `cross_pack_conflicting_rdf_type_aborts_sync_citing_contamination_gate` proves it fires for real: two synthetic packs assert `dom:Widget a dom:TypeA` and `dom:Widget a dom:TypeB` respectively (disjoint output paths, so the pre-existing path-collision gate does not fire), and a real `sync()` call aborts with `[FM-LAW-013]` citing the gate file and the contaminated subject -- before any file is written. Together with the pre-existing `two_packs_colliding_output_aborts_sync_without_rollback_or_lock` (output-path collision), the two conditions named in the prior PARTIAL note (path collision, and term/individual-level contamination) both now have a real, automated, passing check for their tested shapes. Precisely scoped, which is why this stays PARTIAL like condition 9's comparable coverage gap rather than being promoted to ALIVE: (a) the functional-property arm only watches a closed, manually-curated 3-property list (`ccn:principleNumber`, `ccn:mechanized`, `grp:artifactPath`) out of roughly 800 distinct predicate-like tokens across this repo's 28 pack ontologies -- no `owl:FunctionalProperty` declarations exist anywhere in the packs to derive this list from, so it is hand-picked and will not automatically track new packs/properties; (b) the rdf:type arm has no per-property scoping limitation (it watches every subject in the composed graph, not a hardcoded list) but it does carry one deliberate, verified exception: subjects co-typed with `skos:Concept` (the standard SKOS closed-enumeration idiom -- a domain individual doubling as a taxonomy member, e.g. `dfl:Blocked a dfl:Outcome, skos:Concept` in dogfood-lifecycle-pack) are excluded, because that pattern is legitimate modeling, not contamination -- confirmed by reproducing a real 9-row false-positive against dogfood-lifecycle-pack alone (zero cross-pack composition) before adding the exclusion, then confirming zero rows after, and confirming the same exclusion does not mask the genuine dom:TypeA/dom:TypeB conflict the pack_e2e.rs test exercises. Neither arm has cross-pack provenance (the composed graph carries no per-source tagging, `crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs`'s bare `graph.insert_turtle`), so both arms are actually same-subject conflict detectors across the whole graph, not cross-pack-specific detectors -- "cross-pack" in the gate's name/message describes the common trigger case (two packs asserting about the same subject), not a mechanism that distinguishes same-pack from cross-pack origin Re-audited 2026-08-07: `cargo test -p ggen-engine --test pack_e2e cross_pack_conflicting_rdf_type_aborts_sync_citing_contamination_gate` still passes (1 passed, 0 failed); no regression. |
| 9 | 一出力一所有が守られる (one-output-one-owner is preserved) | PARTIAL | Updated: the collision mechanism is now precisely characterized and its remaining gap is narrower and directly evidenced, but the row stays PARTIAL, not ALIVE. `crates/ggen-engine/src/write.rs`'s `resolve_target` enforces target-root containment (absolute paths, `..` traversal, and symlink escapes all refused, `FM-WRITE-002`) -- a real per-write safety check. Separately, `crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs`'s Stage 4 (`generate`) builds ONE flat `Vec<PendingWrite>` from every rendered template in the run -- project templates plus every resolved pack's templates, assembled by `discover_templates` with no pack-affinity tag preserved on `Template`/`PendingWrite` -- then refuses (`FM-WRITE-008`) if any two entries share a `to:` target, via a bare `BTreeMap<&str, usize>` occurrence count, before Stage 5 (write) ever starts. `crates/ggen-engine/tests/pack_e2e.rs`'s pre-existing `two_packs_colliding_output_aborts_sync_without_rollback_or_lock` proved this for two DIFFERENT packs claiming the same output. This pass adds `same_pack_two_templates_colliding_output_aborts_sync_identically` (new, same file), which proves the identical `FM-WRITE-008` refusal -- same no-partial-state guarantees (no file written, no `ggen.lock`, no receipt) -- also fires when ONE pack's own two DIFFERENT templates claim the same output, closing the specific gap this row's prior note left open ("ownership-per-output is not separately audited") for that shape. What remains genuinely unproven, stated precisely: there is no explicit, queryable per-output OWNER registry anywhere in the codebase (`grep -rn '\\bowner\\b' crates/ggen-engine/src crates/praxis-core/src` returns exactly one hit, an unrelated doc comment on `crates/ggen-engine/src/keys.rs:207` about Unix file-permission bits -- no `owner` field, struct, or map exists anywhere) -- what exists is arity enforcement (at most one pending write may target a given path within a single run)