ays so" is entirely manual -- a human or agent runs the command and hand-writes the id/standing/falsifier/evidence row; there is no CI job or script that appends/updates `claims.toml` automatically. Closing this condition fully would mean building that automation (CI-writes-ledger-entry) and back-filling entries for all 20 untracked conditions' evidence -- a separate, unstarted effort, not a one-pass fix; this pass closed one concretely-scoped instance of gap (a) rather than fabricate closure of the whole condition Re-audited 2026-08-07: `docs/aps/claims.toml` now carries 19 `[[claims]]` entries (was 17), and `just guard-claims-schema` exits 0 with real output "ALIVE: 19 claims validated (schema mode)" -- a real improvement. Moves PARTIAL to ALIVE for this condition's schema-mode scope; the automation gap named in the prior note (no CI-writes-ledger-entry mechanism, 20 of 23 conditions still untracked in the ledger) is unchanged and still real, so this upgrade is scoped precisely to "the ledger validates" not "the ledger is complete." |
