| 14 | standing上限が四軸の最弱値として記録される (standing ceiling is recorded as the weakest of four axes) | ALIVE | Updated from PARTIAL: `compute_ceiling` is now genuinely LIVE in the sole production call site -- `crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs`'s `write_receipt` builds `ComponentLevels` from this run's real admission outcomes and passes them through `ReceiptEpochV2Builder`, whose `build()` computes `meet(recoverable(prev), supported(components))` and refuses any ceiling above that meet. Proven end-to-end by the new `crates/ggen-engine/tests/receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs`: a fresh (genesis) project's first real sync receipt records a computed `Green` ceiling, never the `LegacyObserved` sentinel. Two precisely-stated caveats, disclosed rather than hidden: (a) this repo's OWN receipt still shows `LegacyObserved` -- that is now a computed meet OVER a legacy-capped chain (the deliberate one-way cap from the receipted v1->v2 migration, condition 18), not an unwired default; (b) updated: the four axes are no longer forced-uniform -- when the union graph carries admitted `ver:Check` facts (the ggen-verify-pack evidence lane, real exit codes of externally-run commands), `write_receipt` now refines individual axes from that evidence strictly by the meet law (`verify_check_axis` maps each check name to its test/lint/fmt/gate axis; a red non-allowlisted check lowers its axis to Red; a green or `ver:KnownDivergence`-allowlisted check leaves the axis at the admission-derived floor; an axis with NO evidence stays exactly at the floor, never rounded up). Sabotage-proven live: `receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs`'s `red_test_check_lowers_ceiling_and_diverges_tests_class` (a red `test-workspace` check drops the recorded ceiling to Red via the meet while the derived andon honestly stays Green, and a third sync proves Red is monotone) and `allowlisted_red_check_is_recorded_fail_but_does_not_lower_ceiling`. A consumer with no `ver:Check` evidence still gets the uniform floor per `ComponentLevels::uniform`'s documented honesty policy -- evidence-free axes are never fabricated. The recorded value is genuinely the weakest-of-four meet on every live receipt, which is the condition's literal ask Re-audited 2026-08-07: all 13 tests in `receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs` still pass; no regression. |
| 15 | 製品種類別同値関係が全項目に明示される (per-product-type equivalence relations are stated for every item) | PARTIAL | Updated: 4 of the 8 classes are now genuinely EVALUATED live, not merely present-as-Unknown. `crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs`'s `write_receipt` partitions the input-closure hash map into `config` (ggen.toml, project identity, actuator version) and `source` (ontologies, packs, templates, template-declared inputs) via `closure_equivalence_class`, and compares each class byte-hash-for-byte-hash against the previous receipt's closure (`compare_closure_class`): identical -> `Equivalent`; differing -> `Divergent` with the changed keys named in the reason; genesis (no previous receipt) -> `Unknown` honestly, never `Equivalent`-from-absence. Proven by `crates/ggen-engine/tests/receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs`: identical re-sync yields `Equivalent`/`Equivalent`; an ontology edit flips `source` (and only `source`) to `Divergent` naming `ontology.ttl`; a ggen.toml edit flips `config` (and only `config`). Updated again: `tests` and `gates` are now the 3rd and 4th genuinely EVALUATED classes, derived from admitted external `ver:Check` evidence (the ggen-verify-pack lane) -- each check becomes a recorded `ver:{name}` admission item, and `compare_verify_class` compares this run's per-check outcomes (test-axis checks feed `tests`, the non-test axes feed `gates`) against the previous receipt's recorded `ver:` admission items: equal -> `Equivalent`; differing -> `Divergent` naming the flipped checks; either side lacking evidence for the class -> `Unknown` honestly, never `Equivalent`-from-absence. Proven live by `receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs`'s `verify_evidence_makes_tests_and_gates_classes_evaluable` (green evidence: genesis Unknown, second sync Equivalent/Equivalent) and `red_test_check_lowers_ceiling_and_diverges_tests_class` (a flipped test check makes `tests` Divergent naming `test-workspace` while `gates` stays Equivalent). Updated again 2026-07-20: the remaining 4 classes (compiled_binary, docs, receipts, evidence) now each have a dedicated EVIDENCE PRODUCER per its own contract feeding the same admitted ver: lane -- generated scripts projected from packs/ggen-verify-pack ontology facts (templates/produce_docs_manifest_sh.tmpl, produce_receipts_check_sh.tmpl, produce_evidence_check_sh.tmpl, produce_binary_check_sh.tmpl), never inferred at sync: docs emits a path-sorted ver:DocsManifestEntry manifest (sync derives a blake3 identity and compares it against the previous receipt's recorded one); receipts schema-validates receipt-log.jsonl, replays the hash linkage, and records the head (Equivalent ONLY when the replayed head equals the verified previous head the new receipt chains from); evidence checks ver:RequiredCheck completeness plus commit-age freshness over the ver: facts themselves; compiled-binary runs the proven same-host double-cold-build sha256 compare, with --skip emitting an explicit skipped marker so skip and absence stay distinguishable (both keep the class Unknown, but only skip is RECORDED in the admission ledger). `crates/ggen-engine/src/sync.rs`'s `write_receipt` consumes these facts (`compare_producer_class` + a receipts-specific chain-linkage rule), records each as a `class:<class>:<identity>` admission item, and lowers the `gate` component axis by the meet law on any red producer -- never rounding up: red -> Divergent, absent/skipped/no-previous-identity -> Unknown. Proven by `crates/ggen-engine/tests/receipt_genesis_ceiling_e2e.rs`: `all_producers_make_all_eight_classes_evaluated_on_second_sync` (8-of-8 non-Unknown on a real second sync), plus per-class sabotage (`tampered_doc_makes_docs_class_divergent`, `red_receipts_check_diverges_receipts_and_lowers_ceiling`, `green_receipts_check_with_stale_head_is_divergent_not_equivalent`, `red_evidence_check_diverges_evidence_and_lowers_ceiling`, `binary_skip_marker_stays_unknown_but_recorded_and_red_binary_diverges`). Stays PARTIAL, not ALIVE: the equivalence relations are now STATED and mechanically evaluable for all 8 classes, but a consumer that never runs the producers still gets the four classes at the honest Unknown floor, and the generated producer scripts themselves have been proven at the sync-consumption boundary (Chicago e2e over admitted facts), not yet by an end-to-end run of every generated script in a real consumer Re-audited 2026-08-07: `all_producers_make_all_eight_classes_evaluated_on_second_sync` still passes; no regression. |
