## Conclusion

Per 第二十九章's own rule, one unmet condition is sufficient to withhold Level Five publication.

**UPDATE 2026-08-07 (real re-audit, not a version bump)**: condition 18 (migration from old to
new receipt format is itself receipted) now reads **NOT MET** -- `.ggen-v2/migration-receipt.json`,
the persisted artifact this row's ALIVE status was built on, no longer exists on disk (confirmed
by direct read and a full repo search). This single row is, per 第二十九章's own rule, already
sufficient to withhold Level Five publication regardless of every other row's standing. Two more
rows regressed this same re-audit: condition 21 (independently-regenerated distribution artifacts,
ALIVE -> PARTIAL: `book/dist/` no longer exists) and condition 22 (one real improvement passes to
the next generation, ALIVE -> PARTIAL: `.specify/repo-facts.ttl`'s pack inventory has drifted again,
82 real pack directories vs 33 registered `rf:Pack` individuals). Condition 1 also gained a newly
disclosed regression within its existing PARTIAL status (the `marketplace-docs.yml` generation link
was severed by an unrelated PR, `18913354b`). Two rows moved the other direction: condition 10
(required evidence enters only via a formal evidence-carrying path) moved PARTIAL -> ALIVE (claims
ledger grew from 17 to 19 entries, schema validation passes), and condition 20 (reproducible builds)
moved PARTIAL -> ALIVE (a real, live, all-4-target cross-host CI run has now executed and passed --
see condition 20's row for the `gh run` citation). Two rows (7, 16) could not be re-checked this
pass and are marked "NOT RE-VERIFIED this pass" in their own text rather than silently assumed
current.

